@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Theater Seating Chart"; }
<div class="mb-4"><h1 class="hero-title">Theater Seating Chart</h1><p class="hero-subtitle">Select seats to calculate your ticket total.</p></div>
<div class="apple-card mb-5"><div data-theater><div class="theater-screen">SCREEN</div><p class="text-secondary text-center">A–B Front: ₱150 · C–D VIP: ₱300 · E Rear: ₱200</p><div class="seat-grid" data-seat-grid></div><p role="status" class="text-secondary mt-3" data-seat-status></p><p class="output-value-large" data-seat-total aria-label="Total ticket price">₱0</p><p class="text-secondary" data-seat-selection></p><button class="btn-apple-secondary" type="button" data-seat-reset>Clear selection</button></div></div>
<details class="lesson-details"><summary>How it works</summary><div class="lesson-content"><ol><li><strong>Map the seats:</strong> a 5 × 8 array stores selection states, while a matching price array stores the cost at each row-and-column position.</li><li><strong>Assign row prices:</strong> rows A–B cost ₱150, C–D cost ₱300, and E costs ₱200; C4 maps to indexes [2, 3] because array indexes start at zero.</li><li><strong>Toggle a cell:</strong> selecting a seat switches its Boolean value between true and false.</li><li><strong>Recalculate the result:</strong> nested loops visit every seat, count selected cells, and add their corresponding prices; Clear selection empties the selection, and reloading resets this practice chart.</li></ol></div></details>
<details class="lesson-details">
    <summary>C# code</summary>
    <div class="lesson-content"><p>The interactive simulation runs in JavaScript; this C# equivalent highlights the same two-dimensional array operations.</p>
        <div class="macos-code-box">
            <div class="macos-code-header"><div class="code-title">TheaterSeating — core 2D array logic</div><button type="button" class="btn-copy-code" data-code-target="TheaterSeatingArrayCode">Copy code</button></div>
            <pre class="macos-code-body" id="TheaterSeatingArrayCode"><code><mark class="array-code-highlight">bool[,] selected = new bool[5, 8];</mark>
<mark class="array-code-highlight">decimal[,] prices = new decimal[5, 8];</mark>
decimal[] rowPrices = { 150m, 150m, 300m, 300m, 200m };
for (int row = 0; row &lt; prices.GetLength(0); row++)
    for (int column = 0; column &lt; prices.GetLength(1); column++)
        prices[row, column] = rowPrices[row];

// Toggle seat C4: indexes start at zero.
int chosenRow = 2, chosenColumn = 3;
selected[chosenRow, chosenColumn] = !selected[chosenRow, chosenColumn];
decimal total = 0m;
int count = 0;
for (int row = 0; row &lt; selected.GetLength(0); row++)
    for (int column = 0; column &lt; selected.GetLength(1); column++)
        if (selected[row, column])
        {
            <mark class="array-code-highlight">total += prices[row, column];</mark>
            count++;
        }
Console.WriteLine($"{count} selected; total: ₱{total:N2}");</code></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
</details>
